\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The CPSolver iteration loop. The incumbent $\sigma $ is updated only when the comparator judges the new solution better. Section\nobreakspace {}\ref {sec:rl} substitutes only the \emph {Propose move} step.\relax }}{8}{figure.caption.6}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Schema of the Taasika scheduling database, the source system for the pipeline.\relax }}{12}{figure.caption.9}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Schema of the UniTime data model, the target of the pipeline.\relax }}{13}{figure.caption.10}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces The taasika-v3 pipeline. Data flows left to right and top to bottom; the dashed return path is the refinement loop described in Section\nobreakspace {}\ref {sec:evaluation}.\relax }}{14}{figure.caption.11}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces The iterative way of work during the phase. The only manual step is the \emph {Analyse} step; All other transitions are scripted commands.\relax }}{30}{figure.caption.21}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Student violation rate against weight. Open circles are individual seeds and the solid line is the three-seed median. The dashed line is the B0 median, $C = 0.0414$. The medians at weight 0.5 and above lie below that line. One seed at weight 0.5 is 0.0778, above both 0.06 and the B0 median.\relax }}{33}{figure.caption.24}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Hard-check pass rates of the final solution (term Spr11 solution scored against the Spr12 dataset). The vertical axis starts at 85\,\% so that the four checks below 100\,\% (coverage, instructor lunch, student lunch and student conflicts) are legible.\relax }}{35}{figure.caption.27}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Training and production configurations of the learning layer. During training, Python drives three EnvServer workers over gRPC, with a behaviour-cloning prior from SHADOW trajectories; in production the frozen policy runs inside the solver's own JVM and falls back to the stock selector.\relax }}{41}{figure.caption.35}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces The \texttt {scripts/} generators and validators read the Taasika SQL dump (snapshot 242) and create the 16 XML files and archive in \texttt {unitime-out/0gen\_all}. That output goes to the UniTime server (Java 21, Tomcat 9, MySQL 8.4) using CPSolver (IFS + CBS), and also to the headless \texttt {unitime-rl} module with the RL layer. Both solve one XML and write CSV and solver XML to \texttt {solutions/}. The KPI evaluator scores those solutions against the same XML and returns a JSON report.\relax }}{45}{figure.caption.43}%
